A key feature of the group $\Ham(\Sigma,\omega)$ is that it carries a bi-invariant metric, called the Hofer metric \cite{Hofer1990}. The Hofer distance between two Hamiltonian diffeomorphisms $\phi,\psi \in \Ham(\Sigma,\omega)$ is defined as
\begin{equation}
    d_{\mathrm{Hofer}}(\phi,\psi) = \inf_{H} \int_0^1 \left( \max_{\Sigma} H_t - \min_{\Sigma} H_t \right) dt,
